Key Finding — Class Imbalance
------------------------------
Accuracy: 71.5% | Best ROC-AUC: Random Forest (0.767)

Dataset is 70% good credit / 30% bad credit.

Random Forest recall on "Not Creditworthy": only 0.28
-> misses 72% of actual bad-credit applicants, despite
   decent overall accuracy.

Why: model leans toward the majority class under imbalance.
Accuracy alone hides this — per-class recall matters more here.

Next step: class_weight="balanced" or SMOTE to fix it.
